// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.closure (a closure holds what its captures reach, D-0288); conf.closure-captured-slice-source-read
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `c` captures the slice `s`, which borrows `v[0 .. 2]` exclusively, and
// holds it as long as `c` exists (spec/15 §6), so `s`'s borrow lives as
// long (D-0291). Reading `v[0]` while `c` exists conflicts with it on every
// run, as it does for a captured reference. Before D-0291 `s`'s borrow was
// taken to end at its last mention, and `cobc` decided the program.

import std;

fn main()
{
    Vec<i32> v = Vec::new();
    Vec::push(&mut v, 5);
    Vec::push(&mut v, 6);
    auto s = &mut v[0 .. 2];
    auto c = [s]() { s[0] = 1; };
    c();
    printf("%v\n", v[0]);
}
